<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thor</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Donar, Thunor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thor was the Germanic god of thunder, known to the continental <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> as Thunaer or Donar and to the English as Thunor. Armed with his hammer Mjolnir, he was the protector of gods and men against giants and the most widely worshipped god of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scandinavia">Scandinavia</a>. The Old Saxon baptismal vow required converts to renounce him, and his name survives in Thursday.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thor.jpg" alt="Thor" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Max Koch · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_painting_by_Max_Friedrich_Koch_-_Donar-Thor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
